From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: media: describe native SM7675 Iris DMA resources

Describe the control stream, pixel child and four named MMIO resources.
Keep each device's single translated IOMMU domain explicit. Require the
clocks, resets, power domains and interconnects consumed by the candidate.

This binding describes an inactive native driver interface. It adds no
board DT, fixed stream ID or physical-resource claim. Compare Uke OEM
DT94c84aeb and OnePlus SM7675 modules/DT1138e00f separately.

Signed-off-by: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>

diff --git a/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,sm7675-iris.yaml b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,sm7675-iris.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..a312cc0
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/devicetree/bindings/media/qcom,sm7675-iris.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,125 @@
+# SPDX-License-Identifier: (GPL-2.0-only OR BSD-2-Clause)
+%YAML 1.2
+---
+$id: http://devicetree.org/schemas/media/qcom,sm7675-iris.yaml#
+$schema: http://devicetree.org/meta-schemas/core.yaml#
+
+title: Qualcomm SM7675 Iris video accelerator with separate pixel DMA
+
+maintainers:
+  - MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
+
+description: |
+  The control device owns firmware, queues and non-pixel buffers. Its pixel
+  child owns raw input for encoding, raw output for decoding and internal
+  picture buffers. Both devices require separate translated DMA domains.
+  The AON, hardware-fence and timer pages are firmware-visible MMIO mappings.
+  This describes the native resource interface, not a board configuration.
+
+properties:
+  compatible:
+    const: qcom,sm7675-iris
+
+  reg:
+    items:
+      - description: Iris register block
+      - description: Firmware AON page
+      - description: Hardware-fence page
+      - description: Architectural timer page
+
+  reg-names:
+    items:
+      - const: iris
+      - const: aon
+      - const: fence
+      - const: qtimer
+
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  clocks:
+    maxItems: 3
+
+  clock-names:
+    items:
+      - const: iface
+      - const: core
+      - const: vcodec0_core
+
+  power-domains:
+    maxItems: 2
+
+  power-domain-names:
+    items:
+      - const: venus
+      - const: vcodec0
+
+  resets:
+    maxItems: 3
+
+  reset-names:
+    items:
+      - const: bus
+      - const: xo
+      - const: core
+
+  interconnects:
+    maxItems: 2
+
+  interconnect-names:
+    items:
+      - const: cpu-cfg
+      - const: video-mem
+
+  iommus:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description: Non-pixel control stream only
+
+  dma-coherent: true
+
+  memory-region:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  firmware-name:
+    maxItems: 1
+
+  operating-points-v2: true
+
+  opp-table:
+    type: object
+
+  pixel:
+    type: object
+    additionalProperties: false
+    properties:
+      compatible:
+        const: qcom,sm7675-iris-pixel
+      iommus:
+        maxItems: 1
+        description: Non-secure pixel stream in a separate DMA domain
+      dma-coherent: true
+    required:
+      - compatible
+      - iommus
+      - dma-coherent
+
+required:
+  - compatible
+  - reg
+  - reg-names
+  - interrupts
+  - clocks
+  - clock-names
+  - power-domains
+  - power-domain-names
+  - resets
+  - reset-names
+  - interconnects
+  - interconnect-names
+  - iommus
+  - dma-coherent
+  - memory-region
+  - operating-points-v2
+  - pixel
+
+additionalProperties: false
